 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Verdier-duality exchange",
 "statement": "Let $f:X\\to Y$ be a separated finite-type morphism of finite-type $k$-schemes,\nwith $Rf^!$ and the dualizing complexes $\\omega_X=Ra_X^!\\Lambda$,\n$\\omega_Y=Ra_Y^!\\Lambda$ formed with the constructible exceptional adjoint of\n[sk-def-sf-operations](vi) (no admissibility datum is assumed).\nThen $Rf^!\\omega_Y\\cong\\omega_X$, and for $M\\in\\Dctf(X,\\Lambda)$ there is a canonical isomorphism\n\n$$\n\\mathbb D_Y(Rf_!M)\\xrightarrow{\\ \\sim\\ }Rf_*\\mathbb D_X(M),\n$$\n\nin the ambient category $D^+(Y,\\Lambda)$, natural in $M$ and compatible with\nfinite reduction, scalar extension and shifts.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors/sk-thm-sf-verdier-exchange/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-thm-sf-verdier-exchange, order 2503"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-def-sf-operations"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "*Step 1:* $Rf^!\\omega_Y\\cong\\omega_X$: by the composition law and\n[sk-lem-sf-mate], the mate of $R(a_Y\\circ f)_!\\cong Ra_{Y!}Rf_!$ is the\nisomorphism $Rf^!Ra_Y^!\\cong Ra_X^!$. *Step 2:* apply\n[sk-thm-sf-tensor-hom] with $N=\\omega_Y$ and substitute Step 1:\n$\\mathbb D_Y(Rf_!M)=\\RHom_Y(Rf_!M,\\omega_Y)\\cong Rf_*\\RHom_X(M,f^!\\omega_Y)\\cong Rf_*\\RHom_X(M,\\omega_X)=Rf_*\\mathbb D_XM$.\nNaturality and the compatibilities are those of the two ingredients. (This\nproof uses only the tensor–Hom exchange and never the duality chapter, which\nis what removes the proof cycle between the framework and duality chapters.)",
   "uses": [
    "sk-thm-sf-tensor-hom"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
